---
// The "what it looks like" illustration. Made-up, account-neutral details. The answer uses the same
// bullet vocabulary as the worked examples, with its own labels (Progress, Risk, Next step).
---

<div class="chat rv" id="chat">
  <div class="chat-top">
    <span>Illustration: made-up details</span>
    <button class="replay" id="chatReplay" type="button">Replay</button>
  </div>
  <div class="msgs">
    <div class="msg me">
      <div class="who">You</div>
      <p>Here are my notes from this week's workshops. Write them up as the weekly status update, in our standard format.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="typing" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
    <div class="msg ai">
      <div class="who">Coding agent, using an example skill</div>
      <p>Here is the update in the team's standard format:</p>
      <div class="bul"><span class="tag">Progress</span><span>Held three workshops with the operations team and agreed the scope of phase one.</span></div>
      <div class="bul"><span class="tag">Risk</span><span>Access to the test environment is still outstanding.</span></div>
      <div class="bul unc"><span class="tag">Next step. Unconfirmed</span><span>Share the draft plan with the steering group.</span></div>
      <p>I marked the last item unconfirmed because your notes don't say who owns it or when it is due. Tell me and I'll update it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
